  "43tZdDqemein": {
    "proposition_id": "43tZdDqemein",
    "text": "The Lorentz force law tells us that the force on a charged particle in an electric field is F = QE and F = m * (\u0394v/\u0394t) where F is the net force applied to the object, QE is the electric force (in newtons), Q is the charge of the particle, E is the magnitude of the electric field",
    "source_node": "qFTn",
    "source_role": "Knowlegable Expert",
    "confidence": 0.5,
    "status": "belief",
    "scope": "pairwise",
    "dependencies": [],
    "evidence": [],
    "metadata": {
      "round": 0
    }
  },
  "pBWAWQJMoa9k": {
    "proposition_id": "pBWAWQJMoa9k",
    "text": "Therefore  QE = m * (\u0394v/\u0394t)",
    "source_node": "qFTn",
    "source_role": "Knowlegable Expert",
    "confidence": 0.5,
    "status": "belief",
    "scope": "pairwise",
    "dependencies": [],
    "evidence": [],
    "metadata": {
      "round": 0
    }
  },
  "VZMSxgruSg9d": {
    "proposition_id": "VZMSxgruSg9d",
    "text": "Hence velocity (v) times charge (Q) equals to (m * \u0394v)/\u0394t divided by E",
    "source_node": "qFTn",
    "source_role": "Knowlegable Expert",
    "confidence": 0.5,
    "status": "belief",
    "scope": "pairwise",
    "dependencies": [],
    "evidence": [],
    "metadata": {
      "round": 0
    }
  },
  "By7W7wkXP3jb": {
    "proposition_id": "By7W7wkXP3jb",
    "text": "We call \u0394t as (d/v), hence velocity v times charge Q equals to (m * v)/E",
    "source_node": "qFTn",
    "source_role": "Knowlegable Expert",
    "confidence": 0.5,
    "status": "belief",
    "scope": "pairwise",
    "dependencies": [],
